WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.421
Industrial network traffic is a foundational telemetry source.

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:17.220
It shows which devices communicate, the protocols they use, the direction and timing of connections, and in some cases the industrial operations represented by those messages.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:25.364
Traffic at trust boundaries is especially useful for understanding movement between enterprise, site, and control functions.

00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:37.232
Controllers and PLC-related communications can reveal logic transfers, mode changes, programming sessions, and unusual peers when the protocol and collection point provide that visibility.

00:00:37.232 --> 00:00:44.911
HMIs and SCADA applications may record operator logons, alarms, commands, application faults, and communication loss.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:50.263
Engineering workstations offer high-value evidence because they contain privileged tools.

00:00:50.263 --> 00:00:59.338
Endpoint, application, and authentication logs can show users, processes, removable media, project changes, and connections to control devices.

00:00:59.338 --> 00:01:04.225
Collection must be tested to avoid affecting supported applications.

00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:08.181
Historians provide process trends and operating context.

00:01:08.181 --> 00:01:15.860
They can help investigators compare a cyber observation with changes in equipment state or production.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:21.678
Historian access logs and replication paths may also reveal cross-boundary activity.

00:01:21.678 --> 00:01:31.684
Remote-access gateways, VPNs, jump hosts, and vendor platforms should record identity, session times, destination, approval, and sensitive actions where feasible.

00:01:31.684 --> 00:01:39.828
Firewalls and network devices provide permitted and denied connections, configuration changes, link status, and boundary events.

00:01:39.828 --> 00:01:44.249
Identity systems contribute authentication, privilege, and account-lifecycle evidence.

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:48.205
Telemetry quality matters more than raw volume.

00:01:48.205 --> 00:01:56.350
Time synchronization, asset identity, retention, integrity, access control, and clear ownership determine whether records support investigation.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:09.614
Build a source map that explains what each system can report, what it cannot see, how long data is retained, and who responds when the source fails.
